    "body": "_Requested by **Sia**_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Order: independent; safe to merge anytime (follows #432 and #433, already in main).\n- Depends on: nothing open. It edits the same function (`sp-citations--layout-templates`) as #432 and #433, both merged.\n- If merged out of order with the DEVONthink stack (#415, #418-#421) or #426: no conflict expected; they touch other parts of `sp-academic.org`.\n- After merging: nothing to retarget.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Symptom:** the citekey is not in italics (it should be the faded grey italic `sp-citar-key` face: `shadow`, italic).\n- **Cause (found in citar's source and checked in Emacs):** `citar-templates` has no `completion` entry, so citar builds that template itself as `(concat (propertize main 'face 'citar-highlight) (propertize suffix 'face 'citar))`. `propertize` replaces every `face` of the suffix, including the one on the citekey field, with `citar`. citar then reads each field's face from the template at the field's place (`text-properties-at` in `citar-format--parse`), so the key is drawn in `citar`, not `sp-citar-key`. Shown by `sp-citations-citar-default-template-loses-the-face`.\n- **Why it showed up now, not known:** the face was already set this way in #411 and earlier. I could not find a change in #432/#433 that removed it (the pixel cells and the re-formatting do not touch the key's face), so it may have been lost since the `sp-citar-key` suffix was introduced, or it depends on your citar version. I could not run citar here.\n- **Fix:** `sp-citations--completion-template` builds the `completion` entry of `citar-templates` itself: main in `citar-highlight`, as citar does, and the `citar` face added after the faces the suffix has (`add-face-text-property` with append), so the key is `(sp-citar-key citar)`. `sp-citations--layout-templates` now returns `main`, `suffix` and `completion`, and `sp-citations--apply-layout` replaces all three.\n- Tests (`tests/sp-citations-layout-test.el`, 10 pass): the face at the key field of the completion template starts with `sp-citar-key`; the text is main then suffix; citar's default behaviour loses the face; applying the layout keeps one `completion` entry. Tangle check passes.\n- Docs updated in `docs/tangles/academic/sp-academic.org` (bullet lists). No CHANGELOG edit.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Pull this branch, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`) (untested by Claude: GUI)\n- [ ] `C-c w b o` (`citar-open`): the citekey column is faded and in italics (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] `M-: (get-text-property 0 'face (cdr (assq 'completion citar-templates)))` returns `citar-highlight`; the key's face is `(sp-citar-key citar)`\n- [ ] Change the font size (`M-+`), reopen `citar-open`: the key is still italic and the columns line up\n- [ ] Switch theme: the key stays a faded grey in italics\n- [ ] The title and author text looks as before (bold `citar-highlight` main part, `citar` face on the rest)\n- [ ] Regression: `citar-insert-citation` and `citar-create-note` work\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` (`git clean -fd` only after checking `git clean -nd`).\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`.\n- Optionally delete the test branch locally: `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D claude/citar-key-italic` (the remote copy stays until the PR is merged or closed).\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n- No notes or vault files change, so nothing to restore there.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9m8fmtgNiBeMPZDGW)_",
